## 9. Role-creation SQL (canonical artifact)
Save as `aws-access-tools/db-roles/core-1745-roles.sql`. Edit the two `\set`
values per cluster.

```sql
-- CORE-1745 : IAM-auth read-only / read-write database roles
-- Run AS the cluster MASTER user via the SSM tunnel. Idempotent, reversible.
-- Per cluster: community/dbcommunity, eligibility/dbeligibility, offerings/dbofferings
\set owner   dbcommunity
\set appdb   community
\set ON_ERROR_STOP on

-- [1] IAM login roles (idempotent)
DO $$
BEGIN
  IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname='app_ro') THEN CREATE ROLE app_ro WITH LOGIN; END IF;
  IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname='app_rw') THEN CREATE ROLE app_rw WITH LOGIN; END IF;
END $$;

-- [2] Force IAM-token auth (password login rejected)
GRANT rds_iam TO app_ro;
GRANT rds_iam TO app_rw;

-- [3] DB + schema entry
GRANT CONNECT ON DATABASE :"appdb" TO app_ro, app_rw;
GRANT USAGE   ON SCHEMA public      TO app_ro, app_rw;

-- [4] Object privileges — run AS the owner (master is rds_superuser, not a true
--     superuser, so it can't grant on tables it doesn't own).
GRANT :"owner" TO CURRENT_USER;
SET ROLE :"owner";

GRANT SELECT                         ON ALL TABLES    IN SCHEMA public TO app_ro;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON ALL TABLES    IN SCHEMA public TO app_rw;
GRANT USAGE, SELECT                  ON ALL SEQUENCES IN SCHEMA public TO app_rw;

-- Future objects (THE most-missed step — without it, new tables are invisible)
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA public GRANT SELECT                         ON TABLES    TO app_ro;
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA public GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON TABLES    TO app_rw;
ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES IN SCHEMA public GRANT USAGE, SELECT                  ON SEQUENCES TO app_rw;

RESET ROLE;

-- [5] Verify
\du app_ro
\du app_rw
```
> If `GRANT :"owner" TO CURRENT_USER` fails as master, run step [4] while connected
> as the owner itself (`get-to-psql -d community`); steps [1]–[2] still need master.
> If the DB uses schemas beyond `public`, repeat [3]–[4] per schema.

